{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Hard to Understand: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja64'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 64 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Itthivagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Women </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>4. Durājānajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Hard to Understand: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Mā su nandi icchati maṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Do not rejoice, “She loves me,” </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>mā su soci na micchati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>nor lament, “She loves me not.” </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Thīnaṁ bhāvo durājāno, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The mood of women is hard to understand, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>macchassevodake gatan”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>like the track of fish in water. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Durājānajātakaṁ catutthaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
